DataFlow:
Google Cloud Dataflow is a serverless, fully managed execution engine that runs Apache Beam pipelines 
for both batch and streaming workloads, 
seamlessly integrating with Google Cloud services to deliver scalable, real‑time data pipelines.Dataflow is especially powerful for real‑time streaming, 
thanks to autoscaling, dynamic work rebalancing, and Pub/Sub integration

Apache Beam:-Apache Beam is a unified programming model for batch and streaming pipelines.
It is portable across languages and can run on different execution engines (runners). 
Beam defines the pipeline logic, while engines like Flink, Dataflow, and Spark execute it.

PCollection :-Pcollection is a distributed, parallel collection of elements. 
It stores data in the form of elements, which can be either a list, a tuple, or a dictionary

Properties of PCollection:
Distributed & Parallel: Represents data across multiple workers.
Immutable: Transformations create new PCollections, existing ones don’t change.
Bounded / Unbounded: Can hold fixed‑size (batch) or unlimited (stream) data.
Element Type: Elements can be any type, but all must be the same type.
Operation Scope: No fine‑grained operations; transformations apply to the whole collection.
Timestamps: Each element carries an associated timestamp.
Pipeline Ownership: A PCollection belongs to the pipeline that created it; it can’t be shared across pipelines.

--------Ptransform: Ptransform represent a parallel data processing operation, or a step in our pipeline.-----------We use GCS storage in both DF and DP.  
